    expectedAnswer: "A representative DP mock is minimum coin change. Define dp[amount] as the minimum number of coins needed to reach that amount, then build from smaller amounts.",
    deepExplanation: "Step 1 — Understand the interview requirement.\n\nStep 1 — Initialize impossible states with Infinity.\n\nWITHOUT BUILT-IN:\n```ts\nfunction coinChange(\n  coins: readonly number[],\n  amount: number,\n): number {\n  const dp = new Array<number>(amount + 1).fill(Infinity);\n  dp[0] = 0;\n\n  for (let value = 1; value <= amount; value++) {\n    for (const coin of coins) {\n      if (coin <= value && dp[value - coin] !== Infinity) {\n        dp[value] = Math.min(\n          dp[value],\n          dp[value - coin]! + 1,\n        );\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  return dp[amount] === Infinity ? -1 : dp[amount]!;\n}\n```\n\nWITH BUILT-IN:\n```ts\nfunction coinChangeUsingMap(\n  coins: readonly number[],\n  amount: number,\n): number {\n  const memo = new Map<number, number>([[0, 0]]);\n\n  for (let value = 1; value <= amount; value++) {\n    let best = Infinity;\n\n    for (const coin of coins) {\n      const previous = memo.get(value - coin);\n      if (coin <= value && previous !== undefined) {\n        best = Math.min(best, previous + 1);\n      }\n    }\n\n    memo.set(value, best);\n  }\n\n  return memo.get(amount) === Infinity ? -1 : memo.get(amount)!;\n}\n```\n\nExample:\ncoins=[1,2,5], amount=11\n→ 5+5+1 → 3 coins.\n\nComplexity:\nO(amount × numberOfCoins) time and O(amount) space.\n\nStep 5 — Interview takeaway:\nExplain the invariant, complexity, edge cases, and why the optimization is correct.",
