    deepExplanation: "Step 1 — Understand the interview requirement.\n\nStep 1 — Count frequencies, then maintain only k elements in a min-heap.\n\nWITHOUT BUILT-IN:\n```ts\nclass NumberMinHeap {\n  private readonly values: Array<[number, number]> = [];\n\n  get size(): number {\n    return this.values.length;\n  }\n\n  push(item: [number, number]): void {\n    this.values.push(item);\n    let index = this.values.length - 1;\n\n    while (index > 0) {\n      const parent = Math.floor((index - 1) / 2);\n\n      if (this.values[parent]![1] <= this.values[index]![1]) break;\n\n      [this.values[parent], this.values[index]] =\n        [this.values[index]!, this.values[parent]!];\n\n      index = parent;\n    }\n  }\n\n  pop(): [number, number] | undefined {\n    if (this.values.length === 0) return undefined;\n    if (this.values.length === 1) return this.values.pop();\n\n    const result = this.values[0]!;\n    this.values[0] = this.values.pop()!;\n\n    let index = 0;\n\n    while (true) {\n      const left = index * 2 + 1;\n      const right = index * 2 + 2;\n      let smallest = index;\n\n      if (left < this.values.length &&\n          this.values[left]![1] < this.values[smallest]![1]) {\n        smallest = left;\n      }\n\n      if (right < this.values.length &&\n          this.values[right]![1] < this.values[smallest]![1]) {\n        smallest = right;\n      }\n\n      if (smallest === index) break;\n\n      [this.values[index], this.values[smallest]] =\n        [this.values[smallest]!, this.values[index]!];\n\n      index = smallest;\n    }\n\n    return result;\n  }\n}\n\nfunction topKFrequentSenior(\n  nums: readonly number[],\n  k: number,\n): number[] {\n  const count = new Map<number, number>();\n\n  for (const value of nums) {\n    count.set(value, (count.get(value) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n\n  const heap = new NumberMinHeap();\n\n  for (const [value, frequency] of count) {\n    heap.push([value, frequency]);\n\n    if (heap.size > k) {\n      heap.pop();\n    }\n  }\n\n  const result: number[] = [];\n\n  while (heap.size > 0) {\n    result.push(heap.pop()![0]);\n  }\n\n  return result.reverse();\n}\n```\n\nWITH BUILT-IN:\n```ts\nfunction topKFrequentUsingSort(\n  nums: readonly number[],\n  k: number,\n): number[] {\n  const count = new Map<number, number>();\n\n  for (const value of nums) {\n    count.set(value, (count.get(value) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n\n  return [...count.entries()]\n    .sort((a, b) => b[1] - a[1])\n    .slice(0, k)\n    .map(([value]) => value);\n}\n```\n\nExample:\n[1,1,1,2,2,3], k=2\n→ [1,2]\n\nComplexity:\nHeap version O(n log k) after frequency counting.\nSort baseline O(u log u), where u is the number of distinct values.\n\nSenior takeaway:\nBe explicit about tie-breaking, streaming constraints, and why the heap saves work when k is small.\n\nStep 5 — Interview takeaway:\nExplain the invariant, complexity, edge cases, and why the optimization is correct.",
